+   ```
+
+   Bounds are ISO dates or datetimes, UTC unless they carry an offset; `--cwd <substring>` scopes to one project. The script filters each dataset to the window before it projects and writes one file, `summary.md`: coverage, every human prompt of the main agent, tool errors (subagents included), retry loops and slow paths. Each lead carries its dataset, segment ID and UTC time. Done when you have read `summary.md`.
+
+4. Fill each gap from the **live transcript**. The catalog is refreshed from time to time, so recent sessions are absent when the summary reports `LAGGING` or when a session in scope is not in its Sessions list. Read that session from your own context when it is the current one, otherwise from its transcript on its machine (`~/.claude/projects/`, `~/.codex/sessions/`). Done when every session in scope has a source, and your report names each source that is not the catalog.
